## Product OS

Product OS roles and workflows are supplied by the globally installed `product-os` Codex plugin. When the user asks for Product OS, a named Product OS role, or a Product OS workflow, use that global skill to resolve and read the canonical workflow material; do not require a local `product-os/` directory.

All repository-specific Product OS state belongs in `product/`: active runs, hand-offs, decisions, evidence, and memory. Read the relevant `product/active/<work-id>/workflow-state.md` before resuming a run. If this repository has not been initialized, explain that initialization is explicit and use `product-os-init` only when the user asks for it.

This repository's own instructions, coding standards, and approval gates remain authoritative.
<!-- product-os:global-plugin:end -->
